Type: Package
Package: gllvmTMB
Title: Generalised Linear Latent Variable Models with TMB
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R:
    person("Shinichi", "Nakagawa", , "itchyshin@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7765-5182"))
Description: Fits multivariate models for data where each site,
    individual, species, or study has several responses. Start from a
    wide data frame with the 'traits()' formula interface, or from
    already-stacked long data, and estimate trait covariance, pairwise
    correlations, shared latent axes, and trait-specific variance.
    Binary presence-absence applications include binomial-family joint
    species distribution models.
    Optional animal, phylogenetic, spatial, and known-sampling-variance
    components use the same formula grammar. Model fitting uses
    Template Model Builder (Kristensen et al. 2016
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v070.i05>). This experimental package should be used
    through its documented tutorials and model-specific boundaries; convergence
    alone does not establish that an estimate or interval is reliable.
    Broad package-wide interval coverage is not yet confirmed. A handful of
    standardized-loading interval calculations have been checked for one
    Gaussian model, in a few fixed sample-size and rank combinations, and for
    one fixed simulated dataset with known true values. They are only for fits that converge cleanly.
    They do not carry over to other sample sizes, ranks, models, or datasets.
    Total-variance penalty profiles remain
    approximate; agreement with the exact answer has not been confirmed.
